"""Mutations of part 7f's actors (src/game/door.*, supply_box.*, barrel.*) for ../mutfast.py with the
actors build:

    python mutfast.py mutations/mutate_7f.py --models DIR --build build_item.bat --check check_item.py

Each should make check_item.py fail (or the harness crash / hang). Generated from the sources (a
comparison, a number, an operator or a statement per line), then pruned. Left out as equivalent
(82): NormalizeBy's / LengthOf's exact-1 and 1e-8-bit limits and their degenerate branches' sign
tests (< against <= on a component known not to be 0); ties the code never meets (a blend left in
whole steps, an animation end of exactly 1000 ms, allowed exactly 0 in the fall, the slosh at
exactly 2.5, the exit's distances with the entry at the near side); the door's quarter turn in
WriteProperties (the frame's bound centre is in its own space: the turn never moves it, quirk
kept); a return before a branch that cannot match, a motion set to what it is, the close's
autoClose / force (unused for closing), a member set again before use (the morph player replaced
at once, a reset the next call repeats, an S_State already value-initialised, Reset's anim before
SetAnimation's reset, a sound request's defaults); m_unknown94 and the S_State fields ApplyState
never applies (blendTime, anim; animTime only for states the zero state is not); stack garbage
the original leaves (the ReadProperties facing's w, OnMessage's bump position without the tip);
loop bounds only past UB (the door's corner 8, the feet's vertex count + 1, the fall's point 4)
and the holes' delete loops (a leak); RemainingSize > 0 against >= 0 / > 1 and LoadGame's first
id; MSG_DESTROYED's value (only MSG_STATE is compared); =default destructors, a static_assert and
the creators' lambda returns. 24 more did not compile (duplicate case values, enum values) and
were dropped.

Results (2026-10-28): the first run caught 1,096 of 1,620 (24 did not compile, 500 survived): the
supply box's and the barrel's calls were mostly checked by counting single log lines. New cases:
the door's numbers, a new door, CopyFrom, portals beyond 10 m / at 0 / at 1 / a nearer one first,
the other half linked, the closing time, the side with y, handles at exactly 45 and 0 degrees, 1 ms
of the delay or the closing time, the player's height, opening / closing to exactly the ends, the
moving sound in slot 0 and none (-1) with slot -1 set, the volume's centre and inverse, a general
turn, the start's fields, a tiny facing; the supply box's values, a new box, short chunks, more
feet choices, the restart with nothing shown, whole logs of the drop, landing, destruction, the
stop, SetVisibility, the animations and each applied state, the blend's steps, the timer's edges,
respawn 0 and 1, the plane along unnormalised and tiny z axes, the fall onto ground 1.5 m up (the
sweep's, rays' and sphere's arguments, recorded by the fakes, and their lines), the bits' counts,
the parts as the charges; the barrel's tip and sway extremes against the asm, SetDir's directions,
Slerp's flag, the damage's and leak's edges, the surface hit's near side, steep and -z shots, the
bump's points (tiny vectors), the chunks after the hit points, a single hit point. Rerun of the
500: 388 caught; of the 112, 28 more with further cases; of the last 84, 82 equivalent (above)
and two that the tests missed through their own bugs (a blocked step without the rays reset, the
ignore record overwritten by the clearing call). A full rerun: all 1,514 caught."""
